WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.830
Film Courage: When you see people working
harder than you, what does that do for you?

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:06.080
Bill Duke: Inspires me.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.799
When I see people working harder than me?

00:00:09.799 --> 00:00:18.740
I can’t imagine…that…but if I do, it
inspires me to work harder.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:23.769
I mean, good is not good enough.

00:00:23.769 --> 00:00:26.210
And great is not good enough.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:32.180
Excellence….excellence…your name’s on
it.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:38.180
And even if you don’t have the budget you
need and you need to do the best you can with

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.600
what you’re given.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.540
You’re supposed to make 1 million look like
20 million.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:51.220
You’ve got to do it and it takes work.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:55.410
And sleep is not something you do.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:01.180
Film Courage: Were you always like this?

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:11.681
Bill Duke: I had parents who taught me ethics
that I did not know they were teaching me

00:01:11.681 --> 00:01:13.180
at the time.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:25.820
I was very, very young and my father and mother
used to say to my sister and I “Bill and

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.290
Yvonne, always remember this.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:36.440
You’re no better than anybody else, but
nobody is better than you.”

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.850
And they said “Never ask anybody for anything.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:42.450
Go get it.”

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:49.159
My father worked three jobs, my mother worked
two, seven days a week sometimes.

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:54.440
And they wouldn’t take welfare or social
assistance, they were too proud.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:02:02.190
So 
I had hit a low point in New York City one

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:05.090
time and was almost homeless.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:11.960
I literally was getting all the time
with these different things and I was on the

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:12.960
street.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.170
I had my hand out and was begging for money.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.840
And this older lady came by one day and she
looked at me.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.840
And I said “Ma’am can I have some change?”

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.850
And she looked at me and walked by and I thought
she was gone so I asked the next person.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:29.450
And I felt a little tap on my back.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.840
It was the same old lady.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:36.349
And I said “Yes ma’am, you got change?”

00:02:36.349 --> 00:02:44.713
She looked in my face and she said “Son,
do your mama know you’re here doing this?”

00:02:44.713 --> 00:02:48.990
I said “No ma’am.”

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:59.672
She just shook her head and walked away, didn’t
give me a dime.

00:02:59.672 --> 00:03:07.190
I turn around and sat on the steps, I never
begged for money again.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:13.310
Film Courage: Do you still see her face?

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:18.380
Bill Duke: Yes…oh yes.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:25.129
I watched her…she walked two blocks and
took a left and I watched her.

00:03:25.129 --> 00:03:27.569
Changed my life.

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:33.300
It reminded my of what my parents told me.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:37.460
And I had a college education, I had a Master’s
Degree…blah, blah, blah.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:42.920
My mother and father went to the second and
third grade and they never asked anybody for

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:43.920
anything.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.239
I had to carry that legacy on.

00:03:48.239 --> 00:03:49.629
Changed my life.

